    "title": "NWS Birmingham temporarily suspending Routine Weekly Tests - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kaylee Barbee No media credit provided. ,\n6 hours ago\nBIRMINGHAM, AL. (WRBL)- The National Weather Service in Birmingham issued a Public Information Statement Wednesday afternoon to alert citizens of technical difficulties with some of their transmitters.\nThey said that this has impacted their ability to perform Routine Weekly Tests for weather radios and televisions. Some users have reported an “Invalid Location” message on their radio. Some other NWS offices are reporting a similar issue across the US.\nAL Weather Radio Frequencies\nGA Weather Radio Frequencies\nThe National Weather Service is working to fix this issue. In the meantime, they want to inform the public that the weekly Saturday test will be suspended . Routine tests will still be performed at Wednesday at 11AM CT.\nNWS Birmingham also wants to encourage multiple ways to receive weather alerts. This includes weather radios, tv stations, and weather apps (including the WRBL radar app).\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WRBL.\n1",
